Add GND plane on B.Cu and fix net assignment for name-based pins

- pcb_layout.py: nets were looked up only by pad number, so Q1 (B/C/E),
  D1 and D2 (K/A) ended up with no net at all. The mapping now falls back
  to the symbol pin name, resolved to a pad number via the library symbol.
- pcb_layout.py: load_symbol falls back to the sandbox path when running
  under flatpak (the host runtime path is not visible there).
- add_gnd_zone.py: new script that creates and fills a GND zone on B.Cu
  with thermal reliefs. Re-runnable after routing to refill.
- Board regenerated: 75x75 mm, 33 footprints, GND plane, DRC 0 violations
  (63 unrouted items remaining).
- DESIGN.md: layout status and a routing guide; documents that an A* auto
  router was attempted and discarded because at 2.54 mm pitch with 0.2 mm
  clearance the corridors are under 0.1 mm wide and never reached a
  DRC-clean result.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
